From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hermes <hermes@local>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:27:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] host: a family this host does not serve says EAFNOSUPPORT

The trace of the last log opens with socket(family 28, type 1) answered -1 and then the same title's
IPv4 socket: 28 is AF_INET6 (Ryujinx's BsdAddressFamily.InterNetworkV6), and the NPLN clients that try
IPv6 first take their IPv4 path only on a real EAFNOSUPPORT - Citron carries the note that anything else
there "left the whole connection sequence unable to ever complete or definitively fail". The offline BSD
service answered ENETDOWN for every family it did not serve, which is the wrong refusal to hand a client
that is choosing a family.

A family other than AF_INET is answered EAFNOSUPPORT now, and a datagram socket asked for an unsupported
type or protocol EPROTONOSUPPORT, instead of one blanket ENETDOWN.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: The log opens with socket(family 28, type 1) answered -1 and then the same title's IPv4 socket: 28 is
 AF_INET6 (Ryujinx BsdAddressFamily.InterNetworkV6), and the NPLN clients that try IPv6 first take their IPv4 path
 only on a real EAFNOSUPPORT - Citron notes that anything else there left the whole connection sequence unable to
 complete or to fail. The offline BSD service answered a blanket ENETDOWN for every family it did not serve, which
 is the wrong refusal for a client that is choosing a family. Family != AF_INET now answers EAFNOSUPPORT and an
 unsupported type/protocol on a datagram socket EPROTONOSUPPORT.
Issue: https://github.com/GigiFrack/NX2Apple (fork)

---
 dm/host/hle_net.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dm/host/hle_net.c b/dm/host/hle_net.c
index a2ceb0a3..8bdec911 100644
--- a/dm/host/hle_net.c
+++ b/dm/host/hle_net.c
@@ -84,7 +84,8 @@ static int sk_idle(int64_t ms) { dm_guest_sleep_ns((ms < 0 ? 100 : ms) * 1000000
 typedef struct { int32_t fd; int16_t events, revents; } sk_pollfd;
 
 enum { EFD_MAX = 64, SK_POLLIN = 1, SK_POLLOUT = 4, SK_POLLRDNORM = 0x40, SK_POLLWRNORM = 4, SK_POLLNVAL = 0x20,
-       SK_EBADF = 9, SK_EAGAIN = 35, SK_EINVAL = 22, SK_EMSGSIZE = 40, SK_EOPNOTSUPP = 45, SK_EADDRINUSE = 48, SK_ENOTCONN = 57,
+       SK_EBADF = 9, SK_EAGAIN = 35, SK_EINVAL = 22, SK_EMSGSIZE = 40, SK_EPROTONOSUPPORT = 43, SK_EOPNOTSUPP = 45,
+       SK_EAFNOSUPPORT = 47, SK_EADDRINUSE = 48, SK_ENOTCONN = 57,
        SK_NONBLOCK = 0x800, SK_MSG_PEEK = 2, SK_MSG_DONTWAIT = 0x80, SK_UDP = 2, SK_EFD = 1,
        SK_UDP_MAX = 65507, SK_QUEUE_MAX = 1024 * 1024, SK_PACKET_MAX = 256, SK_DEFAULT_BUF = 256 * 1024 };
 
@@ -427,7 +428,11 @@ static int efd_create(uint64_t v, int flags) {
 int dm_sk_socket(int family, int type, int protocol) {
     int tcp = dm_nd_tcp_socket(family, type, protocol);
     if (tcp != ND_NOT) return tcp;
-    if (family != 2 || type != 2 || (protocol && protocol != 17)) return sk_fail();
+    // Which refusal matters: the NPLN clients of several titles open an AF_INET6 socket (28) first and take
+    // their IPv4 path only on a real EAFNOSUPPORT - Citron documents that a wrong errno there leaves the whole
+    // connection sequence unable to complete or to fail, looping. This host serves IPv4, so it says so.
+    if (family != 2) return sk_error(SK_EAFNOSUPPORT);
+    if (type != 2 || (protocol && protocol != 17)) return sk_error(SK_EPROTONOSUPPORT);
     dm_host_mutex_lock(&g_efd_m); int fd = sk_new_locked(SK_UDP); pthread_mutex_unlock(&g_efd_m); return fd;
 }
 int dm_sk_close(int fd) {
